      <p style="color:#4B5563;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 14px;">
        Personal circumstances can change after a POA has been prepared. You may want to replace the appointed representative, modify the authority granted or cancel the existing document.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#4B5563;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:0 0 14px;">
        The appropriate procedure depends on the existing POA and the applicable requirements. Therefore, the original document should be reviewed before making changes.
      </p>
      <p style="color:#4B5563;font-size:0.95rem;line-height:1.8;margin:0;">
        A new document may also need to follow the applicable notarisation or authentication process. Index Office Services can assist with the documentation involved in updating or cancelling POA arrangements.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div style="background:#fff;border:1px solid #B2F5EA;border-radius:16px;padding:28px;">
